{% doc %}
  Shared markup of one product-quiz question, rendered by `blocks/_finder-quiz-question.liquid`
  and `blocks/_recommendation-quiz-question.liquid`.

  Emits two halves separated by `<!-- @product-quiz/split -->` (mirror: blocks/_tab.liquid):
    1. the progress step (bar segment / stepper cell),
    2. the question panel: a fieldset of radio cards (the question's option blocks, or cards the
       runtime generates from the store filter when `is_auto` is on; Finder quiz only).
  `snippets/product-quiz-shell.liquid` resolves the `__PQ_INDEX__` / `__PQ_TOTAL__` /
  `__PQ_STATE__` tokens and the `data-pq-slot hidden` slot, and (Finder quiz, intro off) puts the
  first question's cards in their loading state (`data-quiz-prefetch`).

  Options cannot read their parent's settings, so this snippet rewrites tokens in the captured
  option markup: `__PQ_RADIO__` (the radio name, one group per question), `__PQ_CARD_SCHEME__`
  (this question's `card_color_scheme`), `__PQ_TITLE_SIZE__` (this question's `title_size`, a
  type preset class; the generated-card `<template>` gets the same class), `__PQ_SUBTITLE_COLOR__`
  (this question's `subtitle_color`: `text` | `subtext`, the global `.color-*` helper) and
  `__PQ_IMG_SIZES__` (the option image `sizes`, per image mode). It then cuts ONE fenced part out of the option
  markup (see the option snippet's doc), so each option image renders once. The image mode is
  `custom` only for a vertical card with `image_display: custom`; a horizontal card has no
  Fill/Custom choice (its image is always the left thumbnail), so it is `fill`:
    - Text only: every `<!--pq-media-->…<!--/pq-media-->` part (image, icons, subtitle);
    - Media, mode `fill`: every `<!--pq-custom-->` part (the image stays in the media slot);
    - Media, mode `custom`: every `<!--pq-fill-->` part (the image stays in the icon slot).
  Everything else is CSS on the options grid, so the cards the runtime generates from the
  `<template>` inherit it as well:
    - modifiers: `--media` | `--text`; media adds `--vertical` | `--horizontal`, `--circle`
      (horizontal circle image), `--icon-bg`; either style adds `--comfortable` (`card_padding`);
      `--single` (one desktop column); the selected look (either style) adds
      `--border-background` or `--fill` (`border` adds nothing: the ring is always there);
    - vars: `--product-quiz-image-ratio` (every placement; left out for `adapt` and circle),
      `--product-quiz-image-size` + `--product-quiz-image-size-mobile` (the image width, md+ /
      below md: horizontal and Custom), `--product-quiz-card-border-width` +
      `--product-quiz-card-border-opacity` (`card_border: solid` only),
      `--product-quiz-options-margin-inline` (one column only, with `--single`), and
      `--product-quiz-icon-size` (+ `--product-quiz-icon-color` / `--product-quiz-icon-bg` only
      when set), which size and tint the SVG icon only.
  The card radius rides on the panel (`--product-quiz-card-radius`), with the header and
  card-content alignment (`--product-quiz-header-align[-mobile]`, `--product-quiz-card-align[-mobile]`).

  @param {object} block - The question block (its id, settings and shopify_attributes).
  @param {object} section - The quiz section (its id, progress style and advance mode).
  @param {string} [options_html] - The captured `content_for 'blocks'` (option cards). Ignored
    when `is_auto` is on.
  @param {string} [filter] - Finder quiz only: the store filter (label or param name) the cards map to.
  @param {boolean} [is_auto] - Finder quiz only: cards are generated from the store filter, as
    text cards in the order the filter returns its values, whatever `card_style` is stored.

  @example
  {% render 'product-quiz-question-markup',
    block: block,
    section: section,
    options_html: options_html,
    filter: filter,
    is_auto: is_auto
  %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- comment -%}
  First paint of the heading / subtext: `[question_id]` tokens stripped (see below). Both are inline
  richtext, so these are HTML; `heading_plain` is the heading as text (tags stripped, entities
  decoded so `escape` encodes them once) for every plain-text use, like the stepper label fallback.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture heading_text -%}{% render 'product-quiz-strip-tokens', text: block.settings.heading %}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- capture subtext_text -%}{% render 'product-quiz-strip-tokens', text: block.settings.subtext %}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- liquid
  assign is_auto = is_auto | default: false, allow_false: true
  assign filter = filter | strip

  assign question_id = block.settings.question_id | strip | handleize
  if question_id == blank
    assign question_id = block.id | handleize
  endif
  assign radio_name = section.id | append: '-' | append: block.id

  assign progress_style = section.settings.progress_style
  assign heading_size = block.settings.question_heading_size | default: 'h2'
  assign title_size = block.settings.title_size | default: 'paragraph'
  assign subtitle_color = block.settings.subtitle_color | default: 'subtext'
  assign subtext_color = block.settings.subtext_color | default: 'text'
  assign help_text_color = block.settings.help_text_color | default: 'subtext'
  assign card_scheme = block.settings.card_color_scheme
  assign card_radius = block.settings.card_radius | default: 0 | divided_by: 10.0
  assign header_gap = block.settings.header_gap | default: 24
  assign header_gap_mobile = block.settings.header_gap_mobile | default: 24
  comment
    Generated cards are always Text only, whatever `card_style` is stored. Anything that is not
    `media` (a stale value from an older schema included) renders as text.
  endcomment
  assign card_style = 'text'
  if block.settings.card_style == 'media' and is_auto == false
    assign card_style = 'media'
  endif

  assign heading_plain = heading_text | strip_html | replace: '&nbsp;', ' ' | replace: '&lt;', '<' | replace: '&gt;', '>' | replace: '&quot;', '"' | replace: '&#39;', "'" | replace: '&amp;', '&' | strip
  assign stepper_label = block.settings.stepper_label | default: heading_plain

  comment
    Alignment, per question: header (eyebrow + heading + subtext) and the content inside each
    card. Emitted on the panel as start|center|end so the generated cards cloned from the
    `<template>` inherit them too.
  endcomment
  assign header_align = block.settings.text_alignment | default: 'left' | replace: 'left', 'start' | replace: 'right', 'end'
  assign header_align_mobile = block.settings.text_alignment_mobile | default: 'left' | replace: 'left', 'start' | replace: 'right', 'end'
  assign card_align = block.settings.card_alignment | default: 'left' | replace: 'left', 'start' | replace: 'right', 'end'
  assign card_align_mobile = block.settings.card_alignment_mobile | default: 'left' | replace: 'left', 'start' | replace: 'right', 'end'
  assign align_style = '--product-quiz-header-align: ' | append: header_align | append: '; --product-quiz-header-align-mobile: ' | append: header_align_mobile | append: '; --product-quiz-card-align: ' | append: card_align | append: '; --product-quiz-card-align-mobile: ' | append: card_align_mobile | append: ';'

  comment
    Card style → grid modifiers + vars (see the doc). Media only: layout, image mode + box, icon.
    Image mode: `custom` only on a vertical card; a horizontal card ignores a stored
    `image_display` (no Fill/Custom choice there). Circle (horizontal only) forces 1:1, so the
    ratio var is left out for it, and under `adapt` (natural aspect).
  endcomment
  assign options_class = 'product-quiz__options--' | append: card_style
  if block.settings.card_padding == 'comfortable'
    assign options_class = options_class | append: ' product-quiz__options--comfortable'
  endif
  assign options_style = ''
  assign img_sizes = ''
  assign cut_marker = 'pq-media'
  if card_style == 'media'
    assign card_layout = block.settings.card_layout | default: 'vertical'
    assign image_display = block.settings.image_display | default: 'fill'
    assign image_ratio = block.settings.image_ratio | default: '1/1'
    assign image_width = block.settings.image_width | default: 80
    assign image_width_mobile = block.settings.image_width_mobile | default: 70
    assign icon_size = block.settings.icon_size | default: 24
    assign image_mode = 'fill'
    if card_layout != 'horizontal' and image_display == 'custom'
      assign image_mode = 'custom'
    endif
    assign is_circle = false
    if card_layout == 'horizontal' and block.settings.image_shape == 'circle'
      assign is_circle = true
    endif

    assign options_class = options_class | append: ' product-quiz__options--' | append: card_layout
    if is_circle
      assign options_class = options_class | append: ' product-quiz__options--circle'
    endif
    if block.settings.icon_background
      assign options_class = options_class | append: ' product-quiz__options--icon-bg'
    endif

    assign icon_size_rem = icon_size | divided_by: 10.0
    assign options_style = '--product-quiz-icon-size: ' | append: icon_size_rem | append: 'rem;'
    if block.settings.icon_color != blank
      assign options_style = options_style | append: ' --product-quiz-icon-color: ' | append: block.settings.icon_color | append: ';'
    endif
    if block.settings.icon_background and block.settings.icon_background_color != blank
      assign options_style = options_style | append: ' --product-quiz-icon-bg: ' | append: block.settings.icon_background_color | append: ';'
    endif

    if image_mode == 'custom'
      assign cut_marker = 'pq-fill'
    else
      assign cut_marker = 'pq-custom'
    endif
    if image_ratio != 'adapt' and is_circle == false
      assign options_style = options_style | append: ' --product-quiz-image-ratio: ' | append: image_ratio | append: ';'
    endif

    comment
      Image `sizes`. Horizontal thumbnail and Custom image: the larger of the `image_width`
      (md+) and `image_width_mobile` (below md) px boxes, or its height when a portrait ratio
      makes the cover crop need more pixels than the width. Vertical Fill: one column of the
      900px stage.
    endcomment
    if card_layout == 'horizontal' or image_mode == 'custom'
      assign image_width_rem = image_width | divided_by: 10.0
      assign image_width_mobile_rem = image_width_mobile | divided_by: 10.0
      assign options_style = options_style | append: ' --product-quiz-image-size: ' | append: image_width_rem | append: 'rem; --product-quiz-image-size-mobile: ' | append: image_width_mobile_rem | append: 'rem;'
      assign img_box = image_width | at_least: image_width_mobile
      assign img_slot = img_box
      if is_circle == false and image_ratio != 'adapt'
        assign ratio_w = image_ratio | split: '/' | first | times: 1.0
        assign ratio_h = image_ratio | split: '/' | last | times: 1.0
        if ratio_h > ratio_w
          assign img_slot = img_box | times: ratio_h | divided_by: ratio_w | ceil
        endif
      endif
      assign img_sizes = img_slot | append: 'px'
    else
      assign columns_d = block.settings.columns | default: 4 | at_least: 1
      assign columns_m = block.settings.columns_mobile | default: 2 | at_least: 1
      assign slot_d = 900 | divided_by: columns_d
      assign img_sizes = '(min-width: 768px) ' | append: slot_d | append: 'px, calc(100vw / ' | append: columns_m | append: ')'
    endif
  endif
  comment
    Selected look, either style (generated cards included): `border` is the ring every card has,
    so only the other two add a modifier. Fill picks its surface in CSS from the card's shape.
  endcomment
  comment
    Card border at rest (`card_border`), built like the section border: the CARD scheme's
    `--color-border` at `card_border_opacity`, `card_border_width` wide. Only the width and the
    opacity ride on the grid (generated cards included); the colour resolves on each card, where its
    scheme class defines `--color-border`. Painted by the card's ring overlay, so the selected ring
    takes the same box (see the SCSS).
  endcomment
  if block.settings.card_border == 'solid'
    assign card_border_width_rem = block.settings.card_border_width | default: 1 | divided_by: 10.0
    assign card_border_opacity = block.settings.card_border_opacity | default: 100 | divided_by: 100.0
    assign options_style = options_style | append: ' --product-quiz-card-border-width: ' | append: card_border_width_rem | append: 'rem; --product-quiz-card-border-opacity: ' | append: card_border_opacity | append: ';'
  endif

  comment
    One column (desktop): the grid narrows to 40rem from md up, placed like the header
    (`text_alignment`: start | center | end). Mobile stays full width.
  endcomment
  if block.settings.columns == 1
    assign options_class = options_class | append: ' product-quiz__options--single'
    case header_align
      when 'center'
        assign options_margin = 'auto'
      when 'end'
        assign options_margin = 'auto 0'
      else
        assign options_margin = '0 auto'
    endcase
    assign options_style = options_style | append: ' --product-quiz-options-margin-inline: ' | append: options_margin | append: ';'
  endif

  case block.settings.selected_style
    when 'border_background'
      assign options_class = options_class | append: ' product-quiz__options--border-background'
    when 'fill'
      assign options_class = options_class | append: ' product-quiz__options--fill'
  endcase

  if is_auto
    assign options_html = ''
  else
    assign options_html = options_html | replace: '__PQ_RADIO__', radio_name | replace: '__PQ_CARD_SCHEME__', card_scheme | replace: '__PQ_TITLE_SIZE__', title_size | replace: '__PQ_SUBTITLE_COLOR__', subtitle_color | replace: '__PQ_IMG_SIZES__', img_sizes

    comment
      Cut every `<!--{cut_marker}-->…<!--/{cut_marker}-->` part (see the doc). The fences never
      nest with themselves. `split` drops a trailing empty field, so a segment that ENDS with the
      closing marker has nothing after it: keep ''.
    endcomment
    assign cut_open = '<!--' | append: cut_marker | append: '-->'
    assign cut_close = '<!--/' | append: cut_marker | append: '-->'
    if options_html contains cut_open
      assign media_segments = options_html | split: cut_open
      assign options_html = ''
      for segment in media_segments
        if forloop.first
          assign options_html = segment
        elsif segment contains cut_close
          assign segment_parts = segment | split: cut_close
          if segment_parts.size > 1
            assign options_html = options_html | append: segment_parts.last
          endif
        else
          assign options_html = options_html | append: segment
        endif
      endfor
    endif
  endif

  assign progress_text = 'blocks.product_quiz.progress' | t: current: '__PQ_INDEX__', total: '__PQ_TOTAL__'
  assign next_label = 'blocks.product_quiz.next' | t
-%}
{%- comment -%}
  Header → options gap, per question: fluid mobile → desktop, like the section padding
  (`--product-quiz-header-gap` + `--product-quiz-header-gap-mobile`).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture header_gap_style -%}
  {%- render 'clamp-calculate-style',
    property_name: 'product-quiz-header-gap',
    min_value: header_gap_mobile,
    max_value: header_gap,
    max_breakpoint: 1455
  -%}
{%- endcapture -%}
<!-- @product-quiz/split -->
<li
  class="product-quiz__step"
  ref="progressSteps[]"
  data-question-id="{{ question_id }}"
  data-state="__PQ_STATE__"
>
  <span class="product-quiz__step-circle" data-quiz-step-number>__PQ_INDEX__</span>
  <span class="product-quiz__step-label text-subheading">{{ stepper_label | escape }}</span>
</li>
<!-- @product-quiz/split -->
<div
  class="product-quiz__screen product-quiz__question"
  ref="questions[]"
  data-question-id="{{ question_id }}"
  data-radio-name="{{ radio_name }}"
  {% if filter != blank %}
    data-filter="{{ filter | escape }}"
  {% endif %}
  data-option-source="{% if is_auto %}auto{% else %}manual{% endif %}"
  data-show-in-summary="{{ block.settings.show_in_summary }}"
  style="--product-quiz-card-radius: {{ card_radius }}rem; {{ align_style }} {{ header_gap_style }}"
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
  data-pq-slot hidden
>
  <fieldset class="product-quiz__fieldset" data-quiz-fieldset>
    <legend class="product-quiz__header">
      {%- if progress_style == 'stepper' -%}
        <span class="product-quiz__eyebrow text-subheading" data-quiz-eyebrow>{{ progress_text }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        `[question_id]` tokens: the raw setting rides in `data-template` (the runtime resolves it
        from the answers each time the question is shown); the first paint has them stripped.
        The heading is inline richtext (trusted settings HTML), handled like the subtext below:
        `data-quiz-rich`, raw HTML template, first paint unescaped. Its links stay clickable.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <h2
        class="product-quiz__heading {{ heading_size }}"
        tabindex="-1"
        data-quiz-focus
        data-quiz-tokenized
        data-quiz-rich
        data-template="{{ block.settings.heading | escape }}"
      >
        {{- heading_text -}}
      </h2>
      {%- comment -%}
        The subtext is inline richtext (trusted settings HTML): `data-template` holds the raw HTML,
        the first paint renders the token-stripped HTML unescaped, and `data-quiz-rich` tells the
        runtime not to escape the template (answers stay escaped). Hidden when no text is left.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if block.settings.subtext != blank -%}
        {%- assign subtext_plain = subtext_text | strip_html | replace: '&nbsp;', ' ' | strip -%}
        <span
          class="product-quiz__subtext paragraph color-{{ subtext_color }}"
          data-quiz-tokenized
          data-quiz-rich
          data-template="{{ block.settings.subtext | escape }}"
          {% if subtext_plain == blank %}
            hidden
          {% endif %}
        >
          {{- subtext_text -}}
        </span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </legend>

    {%- if request.design_mode and filter != blank -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Theme editor only: ONE notice per question, in one of two variants (`data-variant`):
        - `warning`: its editor warnings (filter not found / collection too large / manual cards
          the storefront hides);
        - `info`: generated-options questions with no warning, saying where the cards come from.
        A warning always wins: the info text is dropped. Generated questions paint the info
        variant on first paint; the runtime recomputes variant + text from these templates
        (`[filter]`, `[count]` and `[names]` are replaced in JS) and shows the matching icon.
        `t` already HTML-escapes its output: a second `escape` here shows `&quot;` as text.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign notice_filter = 'blocks.product_quiz.editor_filter_unmatched' | t: filter: '[filter]'
        assign notice_large = 'blocks.product_quiz.editor_large_collection' | t
        assign notice_hidden = 'blocks.product_quiz.editor_options_hidden' | t: count: '[count]', names: '[names]'
        assign notice_generated = 'blocks.product_quiz.editor_generated_options' | t
        assign notice_variant = 'warning'
        if is_auto
          assign notice_variant = 'info'
        endif
      -%}
      <div
        class="product-quiz__notice"
        role="status"
        data-quiz-editor-notice
        data-variant="{{ notice_variant }}"
        data-text-filter="{{ notice_filter }}"
        data-text-large="{{ notice_large }}"
        data-text-hidden="{{ notice_hidden }}"
        {% if is_auto %}
          data-text-generated="{{ notice_generated }}"
        {% else %}
          hidden
        {% endif %}
      >
        {%- if is_auto -%}
          {% render 'icon',
            icon: 'info',
            class: 'product-quiz__notice-icon',
            attributes: 'data-quiz-notice-icon="info"'
          %}
        {%- endif -%}
        {% render 'icon',
          icon: 'warning',
          class: 'product-quiz__notice-icon',
          attributes: 'data-quiz-notice-icon="warning" hidden'
        %}
        <div class="product-quiz__notice-text" data-quiz-editor-notice-text>
          {%- if is_auto -%}
            <p>{{ notice_generated }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      The stage stacks the loading spinner over the cards (Finder quiz, intro off), so the cards
      keep their place while it shows.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="product-quiz__stage{% if is_auto %} product-quiz__stage--auto{% endif %}">
      <div
        class="product-quiz__options {{ options_class }}"
        style="--product-quiz-columns: {{ block.settings.columns }}; --product-quiz-columns-mobile: {{ block.settings.columns_mobile }}; {{ options_style }}"
        data-quiz-options
      >
        {%- if is_auto -%}
          <div class="product-quiz__auto-list" data-quiz-auto-list></div>
        {%- else -%}
          {{ options_html }}
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- if filter != blank -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Loading state of the cards while the Finder quiz's first pre-fetch runs (intro off only):
          the shell unhides this over the invisible cards; the runtime reverts both once it resolves.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="product-quiz__prefetch" data-quiz-prefetch hidden>
          {% render 'loading-spinner', size: 'large' %}
          <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'accessibility.loading' | t }}</span>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- if is_auto -%}
      <template data-quiz-auto-template>
        <label class="product-quiz-card color-{{ card_scheme }}" data-quiz-option>
          <input
            class="product-quiz-card__input"
            type="radio"
            name="{{ radio_name }}"
            value=""
            data-label=""
            data-filter-value=""
            data-no-preference="false"
            on:change="product-quiz/onOptionChange"
            on:click="product-quiz/onOptionClick"
            on:keydown="product-quiz/onOptionKeydown"
          >
          <span class="product-quiz-card__body">
            <span class="product-quiz-card__title {{ title_size }}" data-quiz-option-title></span>
          </span>
        </label>
      </template>
    {%- endif -%}
  </fieldset>

  {%- if block.settings.help_text != blank -%}
    <p class="product-quiz__help paragraph color-{{ help_text_color }}">{{ block.settings.help_text }}</p>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="product-quiz__error" data-quiz-error hidden>
    <p class="form-message form-message--error" role="alert">{{ 'blocks.product_quiz.fetch_error' | t }}</p>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn--outline btn--small" on:click="product-quiz/retry">
      <span class="btn__text">{{ 'blocks.product_quiz.retry' | t }}</span>
    </button>
  </div>

  <div class="product-quiz__actions">
    <button type="button" class="product-quiz__link button-unstyled" data-quiz-back on:click="product-quiz/back" hidden>
      {% render 'icon', icon: 'arrow-left', class: 'product-quiz__link-icon' %}
      <span>{{ 'blocks.product_quiz.back' | t }}</span>
    </button>
    {%- if block.settings.allow_skip -%}
      <button type="button" class="product-quiz__link button-unstyled" data-quiz-skip on:click="product-quiz/skip">
        <span>{{ 'blocks.product_quiz.skip_question' | t }}</span>
      </button>
    {%- endif -%}
    <button
      type="button"
      class="product-quiz__next btn btn--primary"
      data-quiz-next
      on:click="product-quiz/next"
      aria-disabled="true"
      {% if section.settings.advance_mode == 'auto' %}
        hidden
      {% endif %}
    >
      <span class="btn__text" data-quiz-next-text data-label="{{ next_label | escape }}">
        {{- next_label | escape -}}
      </span>
      {% render 'loading-spinner', size: 'small' %}
    </button>
  </div>
</div>
